senses.gloss:
प्र-√ तॄ P. Ā. -तरति, ˚ते (Ved. also -तिरति, ˚ते; inf. -ति॑रम्),
to go to sea, pass over, cross, ŚBr. &c. &c.;
to set out, start, RV.; ŚBr.;
 (Ā.) to rise, thrive, prosper, RV.;
to raise, elevate, augment, increase, further, promote, ib.; AV.; ŚBr.; MBh.;
to extend, prolong (esp. with आ॑युस्, ‘to promote long life’; Ā. ‘to live on, live longer’), RV. :
Caus. -तारयति (aor. प्रातीतरत्), to extend, widen, MBh.;
to prolong (life), AV.;
to mislead, take in, deceive, Mṛcch.; Kathās.;
to lead astray, seduce, persuade to (dat. or loc.), Ragh.; Kathās.
